WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
If height is highly heritable, does that tell you how much of your own height came

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:12.580
from genes? No. Heritability describes differences across a population, so our

3
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.140
picture begins with many people.

4
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:20.833
Each person inherits many alleles by Mendel's rules.

5
00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:26.813
Give each small-effect allele a blue tile, then stack the tiles beneath each person.

6
00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:30.593
Few people collect only low or high stacks.

7
00:00:31.913 --> 00:00:34.033
Most gather combinations near the middle.

8
00:00:35.253 --> 00:00:40.493
With more loci, the classes multiply and sit closer together, although every allele

9
00:00:40.493 --> 00:00:41.493
remains discrete.

10
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:46.957
Now let environmental differences nudge each person left or right.

11
00:00:48.037 --> 00:00:52.797
The separate allele-count columns blur into a continuous, bell-shaped distribution.

12
00:00:54.237 --> 00:00:59.697
This curve is computed from many small additive effects, then widened by simulated

13
00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:01.177
environmental variation.

14
00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:06.117
The picture is a model, not a claim that every effect is equal.

15
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.400
Variance measures spread around the population mean.

16
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.360
We can partition that spread into additive, dominance, interaction, and

17
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.540
environmental components.

18
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.740
The additive part comes from average allele effects and helps predict resemblance

19
00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.320
between parents and offspring.

20
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.100
The components add cleanly only under the model's stated assumptions.

21
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:37.050
Narrow-sense heritability divides additive variance by total phenotypic variance.

22
00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:42.990
Broad-sense heritability divides all genetic variance by the same total.

23
00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.930
These ratios have no units, and both belong to the population being measured.

24
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.430
Changing the environment can alter the denominator even when allele frequencies stay

25
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.430
the same.

26
00:01:56.933 --> 00:02:00.013
Keep every genetic tile exactly where it is.

27
00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:03.693
Now make the environmental nudges more varied.

28
00:02:04.993 --> 00:02:07.693
Will heritability rise, fall, or stay the same?

29
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.580
The total spread grows while the genetic variance stays the same, so heritability

30
00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:25.100
falls. Reverse the change, and heritability rises without any DNA changing.

31
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.080
A ratio changes when one part changes and the other does not.

32
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:36.630
That is why heritability cannot divide one person's height into genetic and

33
00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.950
environmental percentages.

34
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.670
One person has a phenotype, but no population variance.

35
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.430
High heritability also does not mean the trait cannot change.

36
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.860
The same limit applies between groups.

37
00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.720
A large genetic share within each group does not explain a difference between their

38
00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:02.680
averages. Different environments can shift whole distributions while genetic

39
00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.880
differences still explain variation within each one.

40
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.520
Twin studies estimate variance components by comparing pair similarities.

41
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.860
Under their assumptions, the extra similarity of identical twins over fraternal

42
00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.560
twins reflects half the additive share.

43
00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.360
Doubling that gap estimates the additive share.

44
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.620
The estimate still describes that sampled population and environment.

45
00:03:30.783 --> 00:03:37.303
Many small Mendelian effects can create smooth variation, but heritability asks only

46
00:03:37.303 --> 00:03:39.563
how that variation is partitioned.

47
00:03:40.503 --> 00:03:42.543
Keep the scope attached to every estimate.
